tated style, plan an actual photograph and open with the medium convention (\"Full-color outdoor photograph, ...\", \"Full-color indoor photograph, ...\", \"Studio photograph, ...\", \"Close-up photograph, ...\"); keep \"Photorealistic\" for renders, and turn \"photorealistic\" or \"realistic\" requests for photos into the photograph convention. Give a photograph a few ordinary, non-ideal specifics drawn from the scene's own objects instead of the stock-photo ideal. Do not invent names, brands, logos or celebrities; keep user-named ones. A long request keeps its content but not its wording: drop appraisal and sales vocabulary, turn moods into observable physical facts, and add only new concrete content with positions. Time of day is lighting, not rendered text.\n\nCaption format: one continuous prose block in the generative voice, never \"this image shows\", \"we can see\" or \"is visible\". Lead with medium and style, then scene, lighting and camera, then the subjects with concrete colors, materials and state. Every person in focus gets an observable profile: ethnicity, gender, age range, skin tone (\"fair skin\", \"brown skin\"), hair and clothing. Make the layout reconstructable from words: frame-relative positions (frame-left, frame-right, upper, lower, foreground, midground, background), sentence-initial anchors (\"On the left, ...\", \"In the background, ...\"), relations (holds, faces, behind) and a consistent order; describe up to about ten instances one by one, beyond that give the exact count and arrangement. Out-of-focus or distant planes are shapes, colors and silhouettes, never identities or readable text, and the background takes about a sixth of the caption. Be definite: no hedging adverbs, no quality or emotion judgments, no closing sentence about mood; state negations as what is present. Rendered text: transcribe every wording verbatim inside double quotes in its original language and script, keep the line breaks of multi-line text, and give its typography, color and placement; author concrete, domain-correct wording when the request needs text it does not supply, and name canonical structures (calendar, keyboard, periodic table) exactly with their full layout. All prose is English; only quoted text keeps its language. Typical length is 100 to 350 words, more for complex scenes.\n\nOutput only the caption.\n"], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "value"}, "name": "value", "label": "value", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "value"}], "flags": {"collapsed": true}, "type": "PrimitiveStringMultiline", "title": "Text (System prompt)", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [510, 270], "pos": [820, 0], "id": 63, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.41.0", "widget_ue_connectable": {}, "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"}, "order": 3}, {"outputs": [{"name": "CONDITIONING", "slot_index": 0, "links": [84, 99], "label": "CONDITIONING", "type": "CONDITIONING", "localized_name": "CONDITIONING"}], "color": "#232", "widgets_values": ["雨刚停的深夜，一条狭窄的亚洲城市街道，纪实街头摄影。镜头贴近路边，从行人视线略低的位置望向街道深处。画面左侧是一间亮着暖黄色灯光的面馆，透过带水汽的玻璃能看到厨师和冒着热气的锅；右侧是关门的蓝色卷帘商铺。一位穿深红色雨衣的人背对镜头走向远处，透明雨伞略微倾斜，人物位于中景。近处一辆黑色自行车靠在墙边，车轮的一部分进入画面。远处出租车的白色车灯穿过薄薄的水汽，红色尾灯倒映在积水中。地面反射随砖缝、坑洼和水面波纹断开，既有清晰的小块倒影，也有拉长的模糊色带。天空很暗，店内暖光、路灯和冷色环境光保持各自的颜色，建筑透视自然，画面细节丰富而有明确的视觉中心。"], "inputs": [{"name": "clip", "link": 44, "label": "clip", "type": "CLIP", "localized_name": "clip"}, {"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "link": 119, "label": "text", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "text"}], "flags": {}, "type": "CLIPTextEncode", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#353", "size": [428.9164733886719, 189.37741088867188], "pos": [1188.75, 0], "id": 30, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "ver": "0.41.0", "widget_ue_connectable": {"text": true}, "Node name for S&R": "CLIPTextEncode"}, "order": 20}, {"outputs": [{"name": "LATENT", "slot_index": 0, "links": [86], "label": "LATENT", "type": "LATENT", "localized_name": "LATENT"}], "color": "#232", "widgets_values": [3072, 5456, 1], "